Messi/Argentina tactical contrast. All material claims are source-licensed. The failures are writer-model violations of explicit drafting rules: the primary source is never cited by its exact title as required by the citation precondition; the lede opens two consecutive sentences with the same banned attribution formula flagged by the near-duplicate-proximity gate; template \"As [X] reports/notes/According to [X]\" constructions appear at least five times across lede, description, summary, and body against a two-instance cap; the closing sentence of the final section is confident abstraction unsupported by specific evidence; and no h2 naturally expresses the demand lens despite the reporting supporting it. All defects are bounded prose repairs; no new reporting is needed.","requiredRepairs":["CITATION PRECONDITION: The primary source must be cited as [Geometry, football and the World Cup final](https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792) â€” exact title as link text â€” before or at the first factual claim. The current link text '[The Conversation]' does not satisfy this mandatory rule.","NEAR-DUPLICATE PROXIMITY (gate: copy-edited, code: near-duplicate-proximity): Rewrite the lede so the two sources do not both enter via consecutive 'As reported by [X]' / 'According to [X]' sentence-opening formulas. The same pairing is reproduced verbatim in the description and summary fields, which must also be corrected.","TEMPLATE SENTENCE OVERUSE: The construction 'As [X] notes/reports' and 'According to [X]' is capped at two instances across the whole article. The manuscript uses it in the lede ('As reported by'), lede again ('According to'), body paragraph 2 ('According to [The Conversation]'), mechanics section ('[The Conversation] notes that'), and tactical section ('[The Conversation] reports that') â€” at minimum five instances. Cut or grammatically vary all but two.","CLOSING ABSTRACTION: The final sentence of 'Tactical methodologies' ('Both sides are prepared to utilize their respective tactical strengths...remaining the primary determinant of the final outcome') is padding without a specific licensed claim. Replace it with a concrete, source-supported observation that opens outward without predicting an outcome.","DESCRIPTION FIELD: The description 'As reported by The Conversation, the matchâ€¦' uses the banned attribution formula and truncates mid-sentence. Rewrite as a complete, natural-language description of approximately 113 characters with no 'As [X] reports' construction.","DEMAND-LENS H2 (gate: standards-cleared, code: demand-lens-missing-h2): Neither '## The mechanics of the triangle' nor '## Tactical methodologies' naturally signals the geometry/football/cup-final demand lens. Revise at least one subheading to express the lens in natural language where the section content supports it."],"report":"## Source Adequacy\n\nThe primary source is Conor Boland's analysis published by The Conversation on 2026-07-17 at https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792. It supplies the geometry thesis in full: the passing-triangle mechanics, the defender-choice forcing logic, the probability-pitch framing, Pedro Porro's 58th-minute goal, the Tex Winter/Chicago Bulls analogy, and MbappÃ©'s post-match \"lack of communication\" quote. All these claims are witnessed in the source text and confirmed in the claim records.\n\nContext 1 (Steve Georgakis, The Conversation, 2026-07-17) supplies legitimate corroborating facts: both sides unbeaten after seven matches, Spain conceding one goal in the tournament, six goal-scorers, the squad's collective character, Messi's role and tactical freedom, Argentina's compact defending, Spain's 2010 title and Argentina's pursuit of a fourth. These are used in the \"Tactical methodologies\" section and are all source-licensed.\n\nThe headline \"Spain's Geometry Meets Messi's Magic in World Cup Final Showdown\" is a reasonable composite of both sources' material and does not invent a frame absent from the reporting. \"Magic\" is editorial characterization within normal practice. No unnamed sources, no invented events, no off-packet claims detected in the body.\n\n## Citation Precondition Failure\n\nThe rule is explicit: \"cite THE STORY as [Exact Story Title](its-exact-url) before making its first factual claim.\" The manuscript's first citation of the primary source â€” in the very first sentence of the lede â€” uses link text \"[The Conversation]\" rather than \"[Geometry, football and the World Cup final]\". This fails the precondition on the first line. The exact URL is present; only the link text is wrong. This is a one-field repair but it is mandatory.\n\n## Near-Duplicate Proximity (Deterministic Gate Failure)\n\nThe deterministic gate `copy-edited / near-duplicate-proximity` fires on exactly these two sentences in the lede:\n\n> \"As reported by [The Conversation](...) â€¦ According to [a secondary analysis](â€¦) â€¦\"\n\nThe same pair of attribution formulas appears identically in the `description` and `summary` frontmatter fields. All three locations must be corrected. The body compounds the problem by adding \"According to [The Conversation]\" (paragraph 2), \"[The Conversation] notes that\" (mechanics section), and \"[The Conversation] reports that\" (tactical section). The article uses this one-trick attribution pattern at least five times, well over the two-instance cap.\n\n## Closing Abstraction\n\nThe final sentence of the \"Tactical methodologies\" section â€” \"Both sides are prepared to utilize their respective tactical strengths to influence the flow of the game, with the question of which side dictates the terms of engagement on the pitch remaining the primary determinant of the final outcome\" â€” is pure placeholder language. It restates the self-evident and predicts nothing specific. The acceptance standard requires prose that is \"specific, useful, non-repetitive, and not padded with confident abstraction.\" This sentence fails on both counts. The sources provide concrete closing material (the speed-of-reconfiguration vs. speed-of-recognition framing, Messi's energy conservation role) that could close the article without padding.\n\n## Description Field\n\nThe description \"As reported by The Conversation, the matchâ€¦\" uses the banned construction and truncates with an ellipsis, leaving it incomplete. A compliant description should be natural prose of approximately 113 characters with no attribution formula.\n\n## Demand-Lens H2 (Warning Gate)\n\nThe deterministic standards reading flags `demand-lens-missing-h2` as a warning. The two h2 subheadings (\"The mechanics of the triangle,\" \"Tactical methodologies\") contain none of the demand-lens terms (geometry, football, cup, final). The primary source's own subheadings â€” \"Forcing choices,\" \"A pitch made of probabilities,\" \"A living network,\" \"The shape that conquered basketball\" â€” all handle the geometry material naturally. Renaming one h2 to reflect \"football geometry\" or \"geometry of the final\" where the section content warrants it would satisfy this gate without forcing keyword copy.\n\n## Structural Observation (Not a Blocking Repair)\n\nThe transition from the geometry analysis (sections 1â€“2) to the Spain/Argentina tactical contrast (section 3) is abrupt; the geometry thread is not carried into the tactical section as a continuing argument. The instructions require each section to continue the previous section's argument rather than reintroducing the event. This weakens the article's analytical coherence but is implicitly addressable by the same rewrite that fixes the other issues.\n\n## Pipeline Diagnosis\n\nSources are adequate and well-matched. The assignment is coherent. The failure layer is writer-model: the model violated explicit, rule-based drafting constraints (citation precondition, template-sentence cap, abstraction prohibition, demand-lens h2) that are independent of the reporting quality. No new reporting is required to produce a compliant draft."}ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;6TQexiJHeA677ZBTO7L5jDm2CYc6KBLJG4vrvcILUKsƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;K8YLi-y0IKVmaq4X8nvjYXqdrMgt6Ri53XFhW3d-wXUƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;hXpuZxrSwgWuv57qN9b0iOaZR4SrnU3vUC6hktLdi98ƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;lityDwnX6vJIniZ-bZjSNkPw9BL03vHuel0GPeh1FlUƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxclaude-code-cli-invocationsƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;-3vbBTT76cRLV_nyoYVqrBtg1qx2LM2QVMY2Qc7cJB4ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka1ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;QsS11d5AmQqzz4453BVDRXCFqY5_HdSzW2Pq-c6cpSYƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkg188.567ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;2oh1oR7zzQunzU-alLMmrxkGq9gF6mmswX17uhGOJwsƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkefalseƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;LWPVdV2-niTuvsF0VxuBo-gwe3KOu3lxmvsjQfAsjMwƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;Jogxdyqxim_PiIRIVryHUMkd1FT63HRWT7PPuVQThtQƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;IEGRNpUqb64pYIUAMyWQrNh3YJIgvJtceBi8PNOs5wAƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxexchange-20260719-152603-8ad716ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;WzOajzFnAp1Jr21HixMx6MI_wZTRPHnRdQUpdUEmEIcƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;YQgYjWpapNNSLass4p5xAwYt1m5oHVoyf8epvd1raKUƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;GO4ehT1EWLaah7YKs1-AycJaxf_hnXrD-aiyr6BqFTMƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkjcompletionƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;DJh43E3UymmJOOu9xirvHrLeVzd-Ne6ZQ5uWssd9isUƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;vG49RebJCy-fc61Q_knxJgJZ57tsPv6RzN-WmBHBRk0ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkd6000ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;rzCqnhsoGf5BkJsMhrvVp1Gqp_INtPzG2KZFLMUrwhwƒdpairƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;YNjAj0TIP0uVJ5_GVu4o3aReNR81k2qQWJ4HSklLsPAƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;twGqxjQ6cS5XkNxNQUh8pA44cPcdL2ndu-CpC-bQzgMƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkz␀ì÷You hold an independent editorial assessment duty. Do not rewrite the manuscript and do not authorize publication directly. Select exactly one bounded customer tool through the supplied schema and put all substantive judgment in the prose report field.

Select submit_editorial_acceptance only when the deterministic standards reading is clear, every material factual claim is supported by the witnessed evidence, attribution is visible, headline and lede are faithful, and the prose is specific, useful, non-repetitive, and not padded with confident abstraction. Acceptance MUST carry failureLayer=none and requiredRepairs=[] exactly.

